cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Citation metadata for this software. The accompanying manuscript is not
  published, so no article reference is given here and no DOI is claimed. Do not
  cite this repository as a publication until that reference exists.

title: "Readout Sensitivity and Temporal Evaluation in Sensor-Based Robot Skill Segmentation for Contact-Rich Assembly"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for a measurement study of proprioceptive low-level
  skill segmentation on the REASSEMBLE corpus. The study quantifies how much of
  the reported segmental F1 is fixed by the annotation and the 5 Hz evaluation
  grid, and how much a change of readout on a frozen encoder moves the score
  relative to adding hierarchical context. Three arms share one encoder: a
  jointly trained GRU with a softmax head, the same frozen GRU with a
  class-balanced logistic probe, and a single-frame logistic regression without
  any encoder. The holdout is the official 37-episode test split, scored once
  under a pre-registered rule that is reported together with the clause it
  conflicts with.
type: software
version: "2.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
